+# The supply-chain policy (step `lakelet/4.22-reproducible-build`): four questions, named here and not
+# answered yet.
+#
+# This is a file a tool runs (`cargo-deny`; `docs/supply-chain.md` says whether it is installed here)
+# and a file a reviewer reads. Each section below is one of the four questions a dependency review
+# asks, and each has to end up carrying the policy *and* the sentence it is there for:
+[advisories]
+# What is vulnerable: a crate with a known advisory, and what a yanked release means for a lockfile
+# that still names it.
+[licenses]
+# What this tree may be built from: the licence families this lockfile actually declares, and anything
+# that needs an exception of its own.
+[bans]
+# What may be here twice: two versions of one crate are two things to audit.
+[sources]
+# Where a crate may come from: one registry, or the build stops.
